[h3]Less Thermometer-Watching, More Delivering[/h3]

A correction from colony management. Our previous note claimed [i]"Late-Game Lag Spikes Were Removed."[/i] That finding was researched somewhat hastily at a basic Research Station, before we had the Data Banks to back it up.

Past Cycle 1000, as it turns out, having Duplicants take the temperature of every loose rock in the galaxy generates enough computational friction to flash-boil Super Coolant.

We have since launched several orbital missions, fed fresh Data Banks into the Virtual Planetarium, and - over the objections of several Duplicants - lubricated the entire delivery engine with Visco-Gel. The delivery system has been rebuilt from scratch.

[b]Changes[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Late-Game Performance:[/b] Duplicants no longer survey every item on the asteroid before deciding where to set down a rock. Each eligible building now keeps its allowed temperature range on file, and errands are checked against the file instead of the asteroid.
[*] [b]Thermo Sensor-Grade Interface Overhaul:[/b] Colony management noticed Duplicants squinting through fogged-up Exo Suit visors at blurry analog dials, accidentally twisting both knobs at once with thick Lead Suit gauntlets. Taking inspiration from the colony's [b]Thermo Sensors[/b] and their crisp, foolproof threshold readouts, the temperature side-screen has been completely rebuilt:
- [b]Independent Bounds:[/b] Distinct "At least" and "Below" rows that never secretly clamp, auto-populate, or fight each other while you type.
- [b]Engraved Units:[/b] Temperature units (C, F, K) are pinned cleanly outside the text boxes, preventing Duplicants from accidentally backspacing the laws of physics. Pasted values with units are cleanly parsed.
- [b]Dedicated Clear Button:[/b] An illuminated [Clear] button wipes limits in a single click - no more hammering the Delete key with an Omni-Tool or deconstructing the bin just to start fresh.
- [b]Live Status Readout:[/b] A plain-language summary line explains exactly what the building accepts at a glance, illuminating in Thermal Overlay warning yellow if an inverted range means no deliveries will ever be made.
- [b]Ergonomic Controls:[/b] Full keyboard support with Tab navigation between fields, Enter to commit, and Escape to abandon typing mistakes before scalding rock gets delivered to your food rations.
[*] [b]Unjammed Colony Steering (No More Swallowed WASD):[/b] For cycles untold, touching a temperature box caused the colony's overhead camera to seize up as if someone had spilled hot Nectar on the controls. Panning (WASD), pausing (Space), and the emergency Escape hatch will no longer get swallowed by overzealous text boxes. Duplicants may still sprint into a magma pool, but at least you can now pan over to watch them do it.
[*] [b]Errand and Warning Decisions:[/b] Delivery assignments and the temperature-aware "Lacks Resources" warning keep pace as the colony spreads across asteroids, space stations, and rockets.
[*] [b]Fast Track:[/b] Runs alongside current releases of Peter Han's [url=https://github.com/peterhaneve/ONIMods/tree/main/FastTrack][i]Fast Track[/i][/url]. With Fast Track enabled, delivery checks ride its pickup system. With it disabled, none of it is loaded.
[*] [b]Fresh Start on Every Load:[/b] Returning to the main menu sweeps out all background tracking. A bin in one colony can no longer be haunted by the limits of a colony you abandoned.
[*] [b]Support Reports:[/b] If something goes thermally sideways, the mod's in-game Options menu will now produce a privacy-safe report. It stays on your machine.
[/list]

[b]Notes[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Your Bins Are Safe:[/b] Existing temperature limits, blueprint construction settings, copied building settings, and saved colonies carry over untouched. The filing cabinet survived the renovation.
[/list]

[b]Known Issues[/b]
[list]
[*] Duplicants still have opinions about which rock is nearest. Unrelated.
[/list]

Every colony is its own lovingly overcomplicated thermodynamic incident, so results will vary. No Duplicants were asked to benchmark molten tungsten.
